  <story>
    <asA>developer</asA>
    <iWant>PRD documents automatically decomposed into individual requirement nodes linked by DERIVED_FROM edges</iWant>
    <soThat>each requirement is independently trackable with its own maturity score and downstream connections</soThat>
    <tasks>
      <task id="1" ac="1,2,3">Implement PRD parsing and requirement extraction
        <subtask>Create /home/ubuntu/scripts/lib/decompose-requirements.mjs for extracting requirements from PRD content</subtask>
        <subtask>Parse PRD document structure to identify discrete functional requirements (sections, bullet points, numbered items with shall/must/should language)</subtask>
        <subtask>Parse non-functional requirements (performance, security, accessibility, scalability sections)</subtask>
        <subtask>Generate unique nodeId per requirement: requirements/{prd-slug}--{req-number} (e.g., requirements/spyhunter-prd--FR-001)</subtask>
        <subtask>Extract metadata per requirement: description, acceptance criteria, priority, related user type/persona</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="2" ac="2,3,5">Create requirement wiki articles
        <subtask>For each extracted requirement, create a wiki article at knowledge/requirements/{slug}.md using the standard article format</subtask>
        <subtask>Set frontmatter: type: requirement, phase: planning, status: active, createdByEpic, createdByStory, tags derived from PRD context</subtask>
        <subtask>Populate article sections: Purpose, Derived From (wikilink to PRD), Acceptance Criteria, Priority, User Type</subtask>
        <subtask>Generate [[wikilinks]] in Derived From section pointing to the parent PRD article</subtask>
        <subtask>If the requirement references existing discovery nodes, add [[wikilinks]] in Dependencies section</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="3" ac="4">Create DERIVED_FROM edges in Memgraph
        <subtask>After creating requirement articles, run graph-sync.mjs to upsert requirement nodes with embeddings and DERIVED_FROM edges to the PRD node</subtask>
        <subtask>Verify edge creation with Cypher query: MATCH (req:Node {type: 'requirement'})-[:DERIVED_FROM]->(prd:Node {type: 'prd'}) RETURN req.nodeId, prd.nodeId</subtask>
        <subtask>Ensure edge weight is set to 0.7 (DERIVED_FROM weight from architecture doc section 6.2)</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="4" ac="6">Per-requirement maturity assessment
        <subtask>Assess maturity individually based on completeness signals: description present (0.2), acceptance criteria defined (0.4), priority assigned (0.5), linked to architecture decisions (0.7), implemented in code (0.9)</subtask>
        <subtask>Store maturity in each requirement article frontmatter</subtask>
        <subtask>Newly extracted requirements start at 0.2-0.4 maturity</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="5" ac="1,7">Integrate decomposition into pre-dev compilation flow
        <subtask>Hook decompose-requirements.mjs into the pre-dev compilation step (Story 4.1) — runs automatically when the compiled article type is prd</subtask>
        <subtask>Handle PRD revisions: diff against existing requirement nodes, update changed, add new, mark removed as status: superseded with SUPERSEDES edge</subtask>
        <subtask>Update knowledge/index.md with all new requirement articles</subtask>
        <subtask>Log decomposition results in knowledge/log.md: PRD nodeId, requirement count, maturity scores</subtask>
      </task>
    </tasks>
  </story>

  <acceptanceCriteria>
    <criterion id="1">When a PRD document is compiled into the knowledge graph (via Story 4.1), a requirement decomposition step runs automatically</criterion>
    <criterion id="2">Each functional requirement identified in the PRD becomes a separate wiki article in knowledge/requirements/ with a unique nodeId</criterion>
    <criterion id="3">Each non-functional requirement is similarly decomposed into its own article in knowledge/requirements/</criterion>
    <criterion id="4">Every requirement article has a DERIVED_FROM edge pointing back to the parent PRD article</criterion>
    <criterion id="5">Requirement articles include: description, acceptance criteria, priority, related user type, and traceability to the PRD section they originated from</criterion>
    <criterion id="6">Maturity is assessed per individual requirement (not just for the PRD as a whole) using the 0.0-1.0 scale from section 6.3</criterion>
    <criterion id="7">When architecture decisions are created later (Story 4.3), they can link back to these requirement nodes via DERIVED_FROM edges, forming the traceability chain: requirement to architecture to code to test</criterion>
  </acceptanceCriteria>

