        <path>docs/concepts/mycelium-labs-architecture.md</path>
        <title>Mycelium-Labs Integration Architecture</title>
        <section>6.2 Impact Propagation</section>
        <snippet>Impact score = edge_weight / (hops ^ 1.5). DERIVED_FROM weight 0.7. When a requirement changes, the compiler traverses the graph and flags all downstream decision and code nodes. Thresholds: >= 0.5 critical, >= 0.1 moderate.</snippet>
      </doc>
      <doc>
        <path>docs/concepts/mycelium-labs-architecture.md</path>
        <title>Mycelium-Labs Integration Architecture</title>
        <section>6.1 Node Status Lifecycle</section>
        <snippet>Status transitions: active (created/refined) to flagged (upstream change detected) to superseded (newer version created) to pruned (no active dependents + deployment passed). Superseded nodes get a SUPERSEDES edge from the new version.</snippet>
      </doc>
