  <constraints>
    <constraint type="architecture">Each requirement is an independent node — not a subsection of the PRD node. This enables fine-grained traceability: requirement to decision to code to test. The PRD is the parent; requirements are children linked by DERIVED_FROM edges.</constraint>
    <constraint type="architecture">Requirement nodeIds must be deterministic and stable across recompilations: requirements/{prd-slug}--{req-number}. This allows diff detection when a PRD is revised.</constraint>
    <constraint type="architecture">DERIVED_FROM edge weight is 0.7 per architecture doc section 6.2. This weight is used in impact propagation calculations.</constraint>
    <constraint type="convention">Requirement articles live in knowledge/requirements/ (a dedicated directory, not under knowledge/planning/) to enable requirement-specific queries and phase gate checks.</constraint>
    <constraint type="dependency">Requires Story 4.1 (Document Generation Compilation Hook) as the integration point. Decomposition hooks into compile-predev.mjs when article type is prd.</constraint>
    <constraint type="dependency">Requires Epic 1 complete (Memgraph, schema, wiki structure, embeddings, graph-sync) and Story 3.5 (Impact Propagation Engine).</constraint>
  </constraints>

